# Nothing personal lives in this repository. Profiles, documents, results,
# exchange rates, the conversion cache and this machine's token are all kept
# in the Flow home, outside it (see server/paths.py). What is ignored below is
# only what a machine produces while running the program.

# ─── This machine ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Points this clone at a Flow home other than the default.
flow.local.json

# ─── Local runtime ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
web/_probe.html

# ─── Scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tmp/
*.tmp

# Regenerable fixture run output
fixtures/_data/

# ─── Where personal files used to be kept ────────────────────────────
# Early versions kept them beside the code. Listed so that such a folder, if it
# ever reappears, can never be committed. tools/check_private.py is the
# second guard: it checks file contents, not just names.
source_data/
data/
.derived/
.agent/
config/profiles.json
config/fx_rates.json
